    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d943">

                <pb facs="0958" n="870" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg870"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 168.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Russell’s No. 225, of November 29 last, containing inclosures of certain
                    documents relating to attachments issued by local courts against the award of
                    the United States and Venezuelan mixed claims commission in the case of Henry F.
                    Rudloff.</p>
                <p>You will advise the Venezuelan Government that the awards rendered by the said
                    commission, in behalf of the claimants, who are United States citizens, are the
                    property of the United States; that the Government of the latter can not
                    recognize the validity of any attachment issued against its property in said
                    awards; that said awards will be collected by the United States Government, and
                    that it will make distribution thereof to whatever parties it may find equitably
                    entitled thereto, and that creditors having claims against claimants before the
                    said commission who are United States citizens would be left to their ordinary
                    recourse before the courts, and that an attempt by the creditors of such
                    claimants to attach the said property of the United States Government would be
                    inconsistent with the comity of States and in contravention of the principles of
                    international law.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
